+++ b/Misc/NEWS.d/next/Library/2026-11-17-00-00-00.gh-issue-XXXXXX.oUwubm.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+Fix :func:`binascii.b2a_qp` and :func:`quopri.encodestring` writing encoded
+lines longer than 76 characters when a space or tab comes just before a line
+break. A soft line break is now inserted before the whitespace, as was already
+done when the whitespace is at the end of the data. The pure-Python encoder in
+:mod:`quopri` gets the same fix. Also fix :func:`binascii.b2a_qp` with
+*istext* false writing a 77-character line when a newline in the data follows
+76 other characters.
